From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: fix three O/H port completeness gaps found by ISA-coverage audit

Patches 0189/0190 gave the O/H port's CC-tree dispatch a genuinely
correct AD target (register readback confirmed: OCCB/OFPNE both
right, input FQ dequeued) but the capture sink still saw 0 frames.
An audit comparing every RX-port mechanism against its O/H
equivalent -- prompted by cross-checking our driver functions against
the full local FMan ISA table (arch/fman-instruction-table.html) --
found three real, concrete gaps in the O/H CC-arm path:

1. fman_port_set_oh_cc_base() never asserted the RM Sec5.12.14.1
   FMFP_EXTC[INV0] SYNC barrier that fman_port_set_cc_base() (RX)
   already implements (F-168/F-215) before dispatch into a freshly
   armed, live FM_CTL-controller-walked structure is safe. fmbm_occb
   is the O/H equivalent of fmbm_rccb -- the exact same class of
   structure the RX comment documents this requirement for. Fixed by
   mirroring the RX barrier exactly, sharing the same global
   fman_cc_engaged_get/inc/dec counter (one FMan controller instance
   backs both port types).

2. fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme()/_clear() (F-162, deterministic
   scheme addressing) were hardcoded RX-only -- same bug class as
   fman_port_set_params_page()'s pre-0190 gap. Extended to branch on
   port_type and use fmbm_ofpne for O/H, same NIA_KG_DIRECT|
   scheme_id[4:0] encoding.

3. THE ROOT CAUSE: no function existed to create+bind a KeyGen scheme
   to an O/H port at all. fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc() and its
   variants all REPROGRAM an EXISTING scheme (found via
   kg_find_port_scheme()) -- valid for RX ports, which always get a
   default RSS scheme bound during normal fman_port_init()
   (keygen_port_hashing_init(), gated on cfg->pcd_fqs_count != 0).
   An O/H port brought up via fman_port_oh_test_bringup() never sets
   pcd_fqs_count, so it NEVER gets a scheme bound. Routing fmbm_ofpne
   to NIA_ENG_HWK (fman_port_set_oh_cc_base()) with nothing bound
   gives KeyGen nothing to select -- the actual explanation for the
   phase-1h MISS. New fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc()/_detach_oh_cc()
   allocate and bind a FRESH catch-all scheme (match_vector=0, the
   documented convention this driver already uses for policer
   pass-through) with next_engine=2 pointed at the CC tree, using the
   same hardware-proven KGSE_MODE recipe (ENQUEUE_KG_DFLT_NIA kept,
   KGSE_CCBS set) the RX attach_cc family already relies on.

cc_arm/cc_disarm updated to call the new attach/detach functions
alongside the existing register-level calls.

Verified via ~/kernel-git-cache/linux (canonical, series-through-0190)
+ git apply --check against a fresh HEAD checkout, all three files
together. NOT YET BOARD-TESTED.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: B (extends two existing
RX-only helpers to a second port type using pre-existing register
fields; adds one new create+bind function and its detach counterpart,
both new/dormant-until-called from the debug harness only; no change
to any existing RX-port behavior or verb)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c | 149 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c   | 111 ++++++++++++--
 include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h                      |  38 +++++
 3 files changed, 285 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
index 421c13a0..de6644fc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_kg.c
@@ -757,6 +757,150 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc);
 
+/*
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc() - create and bind a catch-all KeyGen
+ * scheme routing an O/H port's frames into a CC tree (T-M6-8 Option D
+ * phase 1h).
+ *
+ * Unlike fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()/_dual()/_dual_ekfc() above, which
+ * all REPROGRAM an EXISTING scheme found via kg_find_port_scheme() --
+ * valid for RX ports, which always get a default RSS scheme bound during
+ * normal fman_port_init() (keygen_port_hashing_init(), gated on
+ * cfg->pcd_fqs_count != 0) -- an O/H port brought up via
+ * fman_port_oh_test_bringup() never goes through that path (O/H's cfg
+ * never sets pcd_fqs_count), so it has NO bound scheme at all. Routing
+ * fmbm_ofpne to NIA_ENG_HWK (fman_port_set_oh_cc_base()) with nothing
+ * bound gives KeyGen nothing to select -- the likely explanation for
+ * phase 1h's confirmed MISS despite the CC-tree AD target being
+ * genuinely armed (register readback correct: OCCB/OFPNE both right,
+ * input FQ genuinely dequeued -- but the capture sink still saw 0
+ * frames).
+ *
+ * This allocates a FRESH scheme (kg_alloc_scheme_id(), not
+ * kg_find_port_scheme()) with match_vector=0 -- the documented catch-all
+ * convention already used elsewhere in this driver for a policer
+ * pass-through scheme ("num_extracts==0 ... match_vector is left 0 so
+ * every frame on the bound port selects this scheme") -- so no key
+ * extraction is needed for this minimal de-risk step: the CC tree's own
+ * miss slot (armed with a real hardware enqueue-AD, see cc_arm's
+ * spec.miss_fqid) handles dispatch for every frame. next_engine=2 drives
+ * the SAME hardware-proven KGSE_MODE recipe the RX attach_cc family
+ * already uses (ENQUEUE_KG_DFLT_NIA kept, KGSE_CCBS/kgse_bmch set --
+ * flipping the scheme's own NIA to FM_CTL|AC_CC is proven to stall
+ * dispatch, per keygen_scheme_setup()'s next_engine==2 comment).
+ *
+ * @pcd:           PCD subsystem handle
+ * @hw_port_id:    O/H hardware port id (0x02-0x07)
+ * @cc_group_off:  MURAM byte offset of the CC tree root
+ * @scheme_id_out: out param, the allocated scheme id -- the caller must
+ *                 keep it to later call fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc()
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success, negative errno otherwise.
+ */
+int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
+				  u32 cc_group_off, u8 *scheme_id_out)
+{
+	struct fman_pcd_kg_scheme_params alloc_params = { .id = -1 };
+	struct fman_keygen *keygen;
+	struct keygen_scheme *slot;
+	struct fman *fman;
+	struct mutex *lock;
+	int id, err;
+
+	if (!pcd || !cc_group_off || !scheme_id_out)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (hw_port_id < 0x02 || hw_port_id > 0x07)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	fman = fman_pcd_get_fman(pcd);
+	if (!fman || !fman->keygen)
+		return -ENXIO;
+	keygen = fman->keygen;
+	lock = fman_pcd_get_lock(pcd);
+
+	mutex_lock(lock);
+
+	id = kg_alloc_scheme_id(keygen, &alloc_params);
+	if (id < 0) {
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return id;
+	}
+	slot = &keygen->schemes[id];
+
+	memset(slot, 0, sizeof(*slot));
+	slot->hw_port_id    = hw_port_id;
+	slot->next_engine    = 2;
+	slot->cc_base_offset = 0;
+	slot->cc_bits_sel    = cc_group_off;
+
+	err = keygen_scheme_setup(keygen, id, true);
+	if (err) {
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return err;
+	}
+
+	err = keygen_bind_port_to_schemes(keygen, id, true);
+	if (err) {
+		slot->used = false;
+		(void)keygen_scheme_setup(keygen, id, true);
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return err;
+	}
+
+	{
+		struct fman_port *ohport = fman_port_lookup_oh(fman, hw_port_id);
+
+		if (ohport)
+			(void)fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme(ohport, (u8)id);
+	}
+
+	mutex_unlock(lock);
+	*scheme_id_out = (u8)id;
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc);
+
+/*
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc() - reverse of
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc(): unbind and free the scheme it created.
+ * Idempotent -- a scheme already gone (or an out-of-range id) is a no-op.
+ */
+void fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 scheme_id)
+{
+	struct fman_keygen *keygen;
+	struct fman *fman;
+	struct mutex *lock;
+
+	if (!pcd || scheme_id >= FM_KG_MAX_NUM_OF_SCHEMES)
+		return;
+
+	fman = fman_pcd_get_fman(pcd);
+	if (!fman || !fman->keygen)
+		return;
+	keygen = fman->keygen;
+	lock = fman_pcd_get_lock(pcd);
+
+	mutex_lock(lock);
+	if (!keygen->schemes[scheme_id].used) {
+		mutex_unlock(lock);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	{
+		struct fman_port *ohport = fman_port_lookup_oh(fman,
+			keygen->schemes[scheme_id].hw_port_id);
+
+		if (ohport)
+			fman_port_clear_kg_direct_scheme(ohport);
+	}
+
+	(void)keygen_bind_port_to_schemes(keygen, scheme_id, false);
+	keygen->schemes[scheme_id].used = false;
+	(void)keygen_scheme_setup(keygen, scheme_id, false);
+	mutex_unlock(lock);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc);
+
 int fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id)
 {
 	struct fman_keygen *keygen;
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index 91ab749a6785..0ee2290b715c 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -303,6 +303,43 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 					 u32 cc_group_off);
 
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc() - create and bind a catch-all KeyGen
+ * scheme routing an O/H port's frames into a CC tree (T-M6-8 Option D
+ * phase 1h).
+ *
+ * Unlike the RX attach_cc family above, which all REPROGRAM an existing
+ * scheme (valid only because RX ports always get a default RSS scheme
+ * bound during normal fman_port_init()), an O/H port brought up via the
+ * debug harness never gets any scheme bound -- this allocates a FRESH
+ * one instead. match_vector is left 0 (the documented catch-all
+ * convention this driver already uses for policer pass-through schemes),
+ * so no key extraction happens; the CC tree's own miss slot (a real
+ * hardware enqueue-AD) handles dispatch for every frame.
+ *
+ * @pcd:           PCD subsystem handle (fman_get_pcd())
+ * @hw_port_id:    O/H hardware port id (0x02-0x07)
+ * @cc_group_off:  MURAM byte offset of the CC tree root
+ *                 (fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base())
+ * @scheme_id_out: out param, the allocated scheme id -- keep it to later
+ *                 call fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc()
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success; -EINVAL bad args; -ENXIO no KeyGen; -ENOSPC no
+ * free scheme id.
+ */
+int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
+				  u32 cc_group_off, u8 *scheme_id_out);
+
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc() - reverse of
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc(): unbind and free the scheme it created.
+ * @pcd:        PCD subsystem handle
+ * @scheme_id:  the id returned by fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_oh_cc().
+ *              Idempotent -- an already-gone or out-of-range id is a
+ *              no-op.
+ */
+void fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_oh_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 scheme_id);
+
 /**
  * fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc() - restore an RX port's RSS scheme to the
  * plain BMI-enqueue path (reverse of fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()).
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 1ba6b352626e..17ea7b1678b5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -171,6 +171,7 @@
 #define NIA_ENG_HWP					0x00440000
 #define NIA_ENG_HWK					0x00480000
 #define NIA_KG_CC_EN					0x00000200
+#define NIA_KG_DIRECT					0x00000100	/* F-162 */
 #define NIA_BMI_AC_ENQ_FRAME				0x00000002
 #define NIA_BMI_AC_TX_RELEASE				0x000002C0
 #define NIA_BMI_AC_RELEASE				0x000000C0
@@ -1940,6 +1941,53 @@ int fman_port_set_cc_base(struct fman_port *port, u32 cc_muram_off)
 
 	iowrite32be(cc_muram_off, &port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rccb);
 
+	/*
+	 * F-168 (Task #26, 2026-08-06): RM §5.12.14.1 documents FMFP_EXTC[INV0]
+	 * SYNC as required after changing a live FMan-controller-walked
+	 * structure, before dispatch into it is safe. fmbm_rccb just repointed
+	 * the AC_CC dispatch target; assert SYNC here, before fmbm_rfpne below
+	 * enables dispatch into it -- testing whether this prevents the
+	 * port-wedge that has reproducibly occurred on every prior arm attempt
+	 * this session. Scoped to the arm path only (cc_muram_off != 0);
+	 * teardown (cc_muram_off == 0) is untouched -- it has never shown the
+	 * wedge symptom, so there is no hypothesis to test there. F-167
+	 * board-confirmed this register is safe/responsive to touch standalone;
+	 * this is the first test with an actual port arm in the picture.
+	 */
+	/* F-215(sync-gate): assert the GLOBAL FMFP_EXTC[INV0] SYNC only when
+	 * this is the FIRST engaged RX port on the FMan. A live sibling keeps
+	 * the FMan controller non-quiescent, so INV0 could never clear and
+	 * asserting it on the 2nd port wedges both (image 2040/2129). The
+	 * vendor never asserts INV0 on an arm path with siblings live. */
+	if (cc_muram_off && fman_cc_engaged_get(port->fm) == 0) {
+		const u32 inv0 = 0x80000000U;
+		const unsigned int poll_max = 100000U;
+		u32 extc;
+		unsigned int i;
+
+		fman_set_fpm_extc(port->fm, inv0);
+		for (i = 0; i < poll_max; i++) {
+			extc = fman_get_fpm_extc(port->fm);
+			if (!(extc & inv0))
+				break;
+			udelay(1);
+		}
+		if (extc & inv0)
+			dev_warn(port->dev,
+				 "fman_port: FMFP_EXTC SYNC timed out after %u polls (fmfp_extc=0x%08x)\n",
+				 poll_max, extc);
+		else
+			dev_info(port->dev,
+				 "fman_port: FMFP_EXTC SYNC cleared after %u poll(s)\n", i);
+	}
+
+	/* F-215(sync-gate): maintain the engaged-port counter used above.
+	 * arm (cc_muram_off != 0) -> ++, teardown (== 0) -> -- (floored). */
+	if (cc_muram_off)
+		fman_cc_engaged_inc(port->fm);
+	else
+		fman_cc_engaged_dec(port->fm);
+
 	/*
 	 * SDK FM_PORT_SetPCD concurrence: for the PRS->KG->CC chain the
 	 * parser-to-KeyGen NIA carries NIA_KG_CC_EN so KeyGen hands the
@@ -1966,6 +2014,175 @@ int fman_port_set_cc_base(struct fman_port *port, u32 cc_muram_off)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_set_cc_base);
 
+/**
+ * fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme() - address a single KeyGen scheme
+ * directly in fmbm_rfpne (F-162)
+ * @port: the FMan RX port
+ * @scheme_id: physical scheme id (0-31) to address directly
+ *
+ * SDK FM_PORT_SetPCD's PRS_AND_KG_AND_CC case (fm_port.c SetPcd())
+ * ORs NIA_KG_DIRECT | physicalSchemeId into fmbm_rfpne whenever the
+ * port has exactly one (non-match-vector-selected) scheme bound --
+ * this project's CC-graft model exactly. Without this, the KeyGen
+ * falls back to the generic SI/match-vector scheme-selection walk
+ * instead of deterministically using the CC-attached scheme.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on success, -EINVAL on a NULL/unsupported port type.
+ *
+ * T-M6-8 Option D phase 1h (gap found by ISA-coverage audit): the NIA
+ * encoding (NIA_KG_DIRECT | scheme_id[4:0]) is the same universal FMan
+ * NIA field format used by fmbm_rfpne AND fmbm_ofpne alike -- this was
+ * hardcoded RX-only with no O/H branch, same bug class as
+ * fman_port_set_params_page()'s pre-0190 gap. Extended rather than left
+ * RX-only since an O/H port's CC-attached scheme needs the identical
+ * deterministic-addressing fix.
+ */
+int fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme(struct fman_port *port, u8 scheme_id)
+{
+	u32 __iomem *fpne;
+	u32 val;
+
+	if (!port)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX)
+		fpne = &port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfpne;
+	else if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH)
+		fpne = &port->bmi_regs->oh.fmbm_ofpne;
+	else
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	val = ioread32be(fpne);
+	val = (val & ~0x1Fu) | NIA_KG_DIRECT | ((u32)scheme_id & 0x1Fu);
+	iowrite32be(val, fpne);
+
+	dev_info(port->dev,
+		 "fman_port: KG direct-scheme addressing set, scheme %u (fpne 0x%08x)\n",
+		 scheme_id, val);
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme);
+
+/**
+ * fman_port_clear_kg_direct_scheme() - inverse of
+ * fman_port_set_kg_direct_scheme() (F-162)
+ * @port: the FMan RX or O/H port
+ */
+void fman_port_clear_kg_direct_scheme(struct fman_port *port)
+{
+	u32 __iomem *fpne;
+	u32 val;
+
+	if (!port)
+		return;
+	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX)
+		fpne = &port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfpne;
+	else if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH)
+		fpne = &port->bmi_regs->oh.fmbm_ofpne;
+	else
+		return;
+
+	val = ioread32be(fpne);
+	val &= ~(NIA_KG_DIRECT | 0x1Fu);
+	iowrite32be(val, fpne);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_clear_kg_direct_scheme);
+
+/* F-205 (T-M6-1 Phase 3): parser LCV slots for the hard-parse HXS graph.
+ * Ethernet = slot 0 (universal catch-all), IPv4 = slot 5, IPv6 = slot 6
+ * (silicon-fixed; vendor GetPrsHdrNum). */
+#define FMAN_HWP_HXS_ETH	0
+#define FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV4	5
+#define FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV6	6
+
+/**
+ * fman_port_set_lcv_split() - split this RX port's parser LCV so the ETH
+ * (slot 0, catch-all), IPv4 (slot 5) and IPv6 (slot 6) HXS contribute
+ * distinct bits.
+ * @port: the FMan RX port
+ * @catchall_bit: LCV bit ORed by the ETH HXS (slot 0) — present on EVERY
+ *   frame, so a catch-all scheme (mv=catchall_bit) matches non-IP frames
+ *   (ARP, ND, multicast, L2) that would otherwise NO_SCHEME (0x20000000)
+ * @v4_bit: single LCV bit ORed by the IPv4 HXS (e.g. 0x40000000)
+ * @v6_bit: single LCV bit ORed by the IPv6 HXS (e.g. 0x80000000)
+ *
+ * Zeroes every pmda[].lcv, then sets slot0=catchall, slot5=v4, slot6=v6,
+ * and reads back to verify (S6 R10.2). An IPv4 frame's LCV = v4|catchall,
+ * IPv6 = v6|catchall, non-IP = catchall only. DO NOT zero slot 0 — that was
+ * the 2026-08-19 NO_SCHEME/deaf-port root cause. Enables per-family KeyGen
+ * scheme selection via kgse_mv with a catch-all fallback.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on success, -EINVAL on a NULL/non-RX port, -EIO on readback
+ * mismatch.
+ */
+int fman_port_set_lcv_split(struct fman_port *port, u32 catchall_bit,
+			   u32 v4_bit, u32 v6_bit)
+{
+	struct fman_port_hwp_regs __iomem *regs;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!port || port->port_type != FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX || !port->hwp_regs)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	regs = port->hwp_regs;
+
+	/* The pmda[].lcv words are hard-parser shadow RAM; they only commit to
+	 * the live parse array while the parser is stopped (PCAC PSTOP/PSTAT).
+	 * Mainline init_hwp() and the vendor SetPcd() both bracket every PMDA
+	 * write this way; writing them live lets the register readback pass
+	 * while the live parse memory silently keeps the old value (root cause
+	 * of the 2026-08-19 'split set but slots 5/6 stay dark' board result).
+	 */
+	stop_port_hwp(port);
+	for (i = 0; i < HWP_HXS_COUNT; i++)
+		iowrite32be(0, &regs->pmda[i].lcv);
+	iowrite32be(catchall_bit, &regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_ETH].lcv);
+	iowrite32be(v4_bit, &regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV4].lcv);
+	iowrite32be(v6_bit, &regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV6].lcv);
+
+	if (ioread32be(&regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_ETH].lcv) != catchall_bit ||
+	    ioread32be(&regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV4].lcv) != v4_bit ||
+	    ioread32be(&regs->pmda[FMAN_HWP_HXS_IPV6].lcv) != v6_bit) {
+		start_port_hwp(port);
+		dev_err(port->dev,
+			"fman_port: LCV-split readback mismatch (ca=0x%08x v4=0x%08x v6=0x%08x)\n",
+			catchall_bit, v4_bit, v6_bit);
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+	start_port_hwp(port);
+	dev_info(port->dev,
+		 "fman_port: parser LCV split (ETH slot0=0x%08x, IPv4 slot5=0x%08x, IPv6 slot6=0x%08x)\n",
+		 catchall_bit, v4_bit, v6_bit);
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_set_lcv_split);
+
+/**
+ * fman_port_clear_lcv_split() - restore this RX port's parser LCV to the
+ * mainline default (all HXS lcv = 0xffffffff). Reversibility anchor for
+ * disengage. Readback-verified.
+ * @port: the FMan RX port
+ */
+void fman_port_clear_lcv_split(struct fman_port *port)
